{"id":30540,"artist":"Pearl Jam","title":"Last Kiss","lyrics_plain":"Well, where oh where can my baby be?\nThe Lord took her away from me.\nShe's gone to heaven, so I got to be good,\nso I can see my baby when I leave this world.\nWe were out on a date in my daddy's car.\nWe hadn't driven very far.\nThere in the road, straight ahead...\nThe car was stalled, the engine was dead.\nI couldn't stop, so I swerved to the right.\nNever forget the sound that night...\nThe cryin' tires, the bustin' glass.\nThe painful scream that I heard last.\nWell, where oh where can my baby be?\nThe Lord took her away from me.\nShe's gone to heaven, so I got to be good,\nso I can see my baby when I leave this world.\nWell, when I woke up, the rain was pourin' down.\nThere were people standing all around.\nSomething warm running in my eyes,\nbut I found my baby somehow that night.\nI raised her head, and when she smiled, and said,\n\"Hold me darling for a little while.\"\nI held her close. I kissed her our last kiss.\nI found the love that I knew I would miss.\nBut now she's gone, even though I hold her tight.\nI lost my love... my life, that night.\nWell, where oh where can my baby be?\nThe Lord took her away from me.\nShe's gone to heaven, so I got to be good,\nso I can see my baby when I leave this world.\nOoooh Oooooh\nOoooh Oooooh\nOoooh Oooooh\nOoooh Oooooh","lyrics_synced":"[00:15.00] Well, where oh where can my baby be?\n[00:19.07] The Lord took her away from me.\n[00:22.50] She's gone to heaven, so I got to be good,\n[00:25.50] so I can see my baby when I leave this world.\n[00:32.14] We were out on a date in my daddy's car.\n[00:36.21] We hadn't driven very far.\n[00:39.43] There in the road, straight ahead...\n[00:43.07] The car was stalled, the engine was dead.\n[00:46.29] I couldn't stop, so I swerved to the right.\n[00:49.71] Never forget the sound that night...\n[00:52.93] The cryin' tires, the bustin' glass.\n[00:56.36] The painful scream that I heard last.\n[01:03.00] Well